<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Pollilur (1780)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10 September <a href="/years/1780">1780</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · <a href="/today-in-history/september-10">On this day: 10 September</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-mysore-war">Second Anglo-Mysore War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Pollilur was fought on 10 September 1780 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a> in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-mysore-war">Second Anglo-Mysore War</a>. Forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> surrounded and destroyed a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> detachment under Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-baillie">William Baillie</a>, most of whose men were killed or captured. It was one of the worst defeats suffered by the Company in India, later celebrated in a mural at Tipu's summer palace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-pollilur-1780.jpg" alt="Battle of Pollilur (1780)" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles H. Hubbell (1898-1971) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rocket_warfare.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Second Anglo-Mysore War (1780–1784) his army destroyed a British detachment under William Baillie at <b>Pollilur</b> in 1780, though Eyre Coote defeated him at Porto Novo in 1781.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore (1399-1799) · Military</a></li></ul></section>
